---
description: |
  Parse Palo Alto Networks PAN-OS syslog CSV payloads.

  PAN-OS writes most times, such as the generated and receive times, without a
  zone, in the time zone of the firewall. The parser interprets them in the
  `timezone` argument when you set it. Otherwise it uses the UTC offset of the
  record's high-resolution timestamp, which PAN-OS writes with an offset, and
  falls back to UTC. An IANA time zone name accounts for daylight saving time
  per record. A fixed offset, such as `+01:00`, doesn't: records from both
  sides of a daylight saving change then need different offsets, which the
  high-resolution timestamp provides.
args:
  positional:
    - name: input
      type: field
      description: The source field to parse.
    - name: paloalto
      type: field
      description: The field that receives the parsed event.
  named:
    - name: timezone
      type: string
      default: null
      description: |
        The time zone of times without a zone, as an IANA name such as
        `Europe/Berlin` or as a UTC offset such as `+01:00`.
---

// Header constants are derived from Palo Alto Networks' syslog field
// description pages. The raw payload is a CSV string whose fourth field is the
// log type and whose fifth field is the subtype for several log families.
// Source: https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/traffic-log-fields
